    {
      "bbox": [
        141,
        1512,
        1750,
        1770
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "7-Volunteers much prefer working in their own neighborhoods. Brooklyn, Queens, the Bronx, and Richmond have proved more difficult problems with regard to finding volunteer opportunities than has Manhattan. City agencies, such as the Police and Fire Department, have divisions in every city neighborhood can prove invaluable in solving this problem.",
