        1970,
        1772,
        2230
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "9-Certain agencies train or orient the H.S. students assigned to their agency. In some cases, the sink or swim approach is used. Volunteers tend to be more effective and better integrated into their jobs when they receive at least a minimal orientation. This can be accomplished by orienting monthly or bi-monthly all students who have been referred during that time period.",
